From: Prithwiraj Samanta <app@datainsights.ae>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:11:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] telecode: attach the automation bridge to the embedding
 proxy

Upstream connects the MCP/automation bridge only in dev builds or the
desktop app, where it can spawn openpencil-mcp-http. When the editor is
embedded by telecode (?project=<id>) the server side of the same
register/request/response protocol is the proxy's
/api/design/editor-bridge WebSocket, so production web builds attach to
it too. The bridge URL is always same-origin (a ?bridge= override is only
honoured for this host) and the token comes from ?bridge_token= or the
td-bridge-token meta tag the proxy injects into index.html.
